    "ledger": {
      "$description": "Every generated token is a proposal; src/theme/ledger.json records what people decided. proposed = unreviewed, ships as generated. kept = reviewed and wanted. cut = collapses to its fallback everywhere; the fallback is named on the token. Agents: never reach for a cut token; to cut or keep one, run npm run ledger -- cut|keep <token> --why \"…\".",
      "source": "src/theme/ledger.json",
      "counts": {
        "proposed": 13,
        "kept": 31,
        "cut": 3
      },
      "cut": [
        {
          "token": "--shadow-color",
          "fallback": "transparent",
          "decided": {
            "kind": "human",
            "actor": "prometheus-000"
          },
          "reason": "Lines, not shadows. The reference grammar — the portfolio and Visionary alike — draws every level with a 1px rule and an alpha wash, and paints no drop shadow anywhere; a shadow is decoration the eye pays for on every card. The elevation tokens keep their offsets and paint nothing, so the rule does the work it was already doing."
        },
        {
          "token": "--motion-ease-emphasis",
          "fallback": "--motion-ease",
          "decided": {
            "kind": "human",
            "actor": "prometheus-000"
          },
          "reason": "Nothing bounces. The engine gives a calm theme a spring on emphasis above energy 0.3, and a dialog that overshoots is a personality the chrome should not have. Collapses to the ordinary curve; the energy dial still sets speed."
        },
        {
          "token": "--radius-overlay",
          "fallback": "--radius-surface",
          "decided": {
            "kind": "human",
            "actor": "prometheus-000"
          },
          "reason": "Two radii, not three: a control and a panel. The engine gave overlays 2.4× the control radius, which at calm energy is a 19px dialog — the one soft shape on an otherwise architectural page. An overlay is a panel; it rounds like one."
        }
      ]
    },
